92: Our Advertising Services
93: This section describes the information we collect, use, and share through our Advertising Services.
94: General Information Collection and Use
95: If you are a consumer who downloads and uses an application which contains the AppLovin SDK or otherwise interacts with the Services through advertisements served within a digital property, we may collect certain information, including the following:
96: Device, App, and Browser Data
97: Device make, model, hardware, and operating system;
98: Device properties related to screen, display, size, orientation, audio, video, battery, storage, memory usage, settings, and boot time;
99: Device settings related to accessibility features and font size;
100: Device integrity and security signals;
101: Carrier;
102: Name, properties, performance, session information, and installation information of the mobile application through which you interact with the Services;
103: Country, time zone, and locale settings (country and preferred language);
104: Network connection type and speed;
105: IP Address;
106: Internet browser user-agent and software environment used to access the Services;
107: HTTP header and request information;
108: Advertising IDs (IDFA/GAID/Amazon Advertising ID);
109: Vendor IDs (IDFV);
110: App Set IDs;
111: Email addresses, phone numbers, and Publisher User IDs (if provided by publisher); and
112: Advertising and tracking preferences and restrictions.
113: Advertisers (through the advertiser itself or through a third party service provider on behalf of such advertiser) may also share transactional or other “event” data related to a consumer’s interaction with an application, such as information about purchases or application installations.
